{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Job</b> — He was among the descendants of Nahor, brother of Abraham. And what seems correct to me: that he was among the descendants of Esau, and the matter is proven by [the phrase] 'in the land of Uz,' as in: [Lamentations 4:21], 'Rejoice and be glad, O daughter of Edom, who dwells in the land of Uz.' And it is impossible to say that he never existed, because Ezekiel said: 'Noah, Daniel, and Job' [Ezekiel 14:14]. And if a disputant says: perhaps it was a different Job that the prophet mentioned? One shall answer him: if so, say the same about Daniel and Noah. And behold, it is written in another verse: 'Though Moses and Samuel stood before Me' [Jeremiah 15:1] — and we find Samuel [son] of Amihud, and we do not find any other Job written in the holy books. And the one who says he is Jobab son of Zerah of Bozrah [Genesis 36:33] — perhaps he saw this in a dream, for he has nothing to rely on, neither on the words of the prophets nor on what our Sages of blessed memory transmitted. And do not wonder about the word 'Job' as his name, for he is not wicked at all — and behold it is written: 'YHWH is a man of war, YHWH is His name' [Exodus 15:3]. And the opposite of the matter: 'There was a certain man from the hill country of Ephraim, and his name was Micaiah' [1 Kings 22:8]. Perhaps the author of the midrash [located] the place of Job near Haran, on account of [Genesis 29:1], 'he went to the land of the children of the east.'"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The citation from 1 Kings 22:8 gives 'Micaiah' (מיכיהו) as a counterexample of a name whose meaning does not match the person's character; the verse reference is resolved by inference from the quoted phrase. The closing sentence appears slightly elliptical; translated hyper-literally as the syntax stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:32.804716579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}